WEBVTT

00:01.091 --> 00:02.466
[ELSIE] Quests that pay well

00:02.467 --> 00:04.969
carry a whole new level
of difficulty and danger.

00:04.970 --> 00:06.512
You still want to do this?

00:06.513 --> 00:07.847
Heck yeah.

00:07.848 --> 00:10.266
Elsie, I'm able to fight now.

00:10.267 --> 00:13.144
Plus we have Rein's enchantments
to give us a nice boost.

00:13.145 --> 00:16.647
We'll recruit party members.
We know some people.

00:16.648 --> 00:19.900
You can depend on us.
We'll make it through this.

00:19.901 --> 00:21.153
[gasps softly]

00:22.070 --> 00:23.030
[chuckles]

00:23.405 --> 00:25.823
[OLD MAN] I originally offered
three million.

00:25.824 --> 00:27.158
[ELSIE] But not anymore?

00:27.159 --> 00:29.493
[OLD MAN] The first round
of adventurers died,

00:29.494 --> 00:31.787
so I raised the reward to 20.

00:31.788 --> 00:34.040
Then the village
where I offered the job

00:34.041 --> 00:35.249
got wiped out,

00:35.250 --> 00:37.626
so now I'm reaching out
to the neighboring ones

00:37.627 --> 00:38.919
with a new price:

00:38.920 --> 00:41.590
One hundred and seventy million.

00:42.090 --> 00:43.592
That's a start.

00:44.426 --> 00:45.634
What'll it be?

00:45.635 --> 00:46.887
- [customers cheering]
- Mm?

00:47.596 --> 00:49.138
[CUSTOMER 1]
Can any of you tell me

00:49.139 --> 00:51.682
why the Beast's Fangs,
one of the big five guilds,

00:51.683 --> 00:52.767
fell like a house of cards?

00:52.768 --> 00:55.102
I heard someone cursed
their gear making it weak!

00:55.103 --> 00:57.521
Turns out the entire operation
was just a scam.

00:57.522 --> 01:00.066
And their vice guildmaster
vanished without a trace!

01:00.067 --> 01:03.444
I seem to be hearing that
everywhere I go as of late.

01:03.445 --> 01:04.445
[ELSIE] Hmm.

01:04.446 --> 01:05.780
[CUSTOMER 1]
Get a load of this new theory.

01:05.781 --> 01:07.198
The secret to their success

01:07.199 --> 01:08.824
was that enchanter
they had on staff.

01:08.825 --> 01:10.451
But he dispelled
all the enchantments

01:10.452 --> 01:11.702
on their gear and quit.

01:11.703 --> 01:14.246
- That's why they collapsed.
- [CUSTOMER 2] Huh? No way.

01:14.247 --> 01:15.873
[CUSTOMER 3] Yeah, right.

01:15.874 --> 01:17.958
[ELSIE]
<i>If rumors about Rein spread,</i>

01:17.959 --> 01:20.628
<i>all sorts of people
will try to track him down,</i>

01:20.629 --> 01:22.755
<i>including the worst
of the worst.</i>

01:22.756 --> 01:24.215
<i>The ones that'd brainwash him</i>

01:24.216 --> 01:26.176
<i>and force him
to enchant their gear.</i>

01:26.843 --> 01:29.136
Anyway, have you already heard

01:29.137 --> 01:31.597
- the news about Cornelius?
- Hm?

01:31.598 --> 01:33.599
[OLD MAN] He let it slip
that he killed Glenda,

01:33.600 --> 01:36.018
vice guildmaster
of the Beast's Fangs.

01:36.019 --> 01:37.603
Unfortunately for Cornelius,

01:37.604 --> 01:39.980
there's a man who loved her
like his own mother.

01:39.981 --> 01:42.484
Oh? And does he have a name?

01:43.110 --> 01:44.985
They call him Half.

01:44.986 --> 01:47.154
<i>On account of him
always telling people</i>

01:47.155 --> 01:50.325
<i>he was incomplete
and Glenda was his other half.</i>

01:51.118 --> 01:53.119
<i>The people have come up
with a name for the group</i>

01:53.120 --> 01:55.871
<i>that left the Beast's Fangs
alongside him</i>

01:55.872 --> 01:59.334
<i>and now rule the streets
by force and intimidation.</i>

02:00.794 --> 02:02.421
The THUGs.

02:04.005 --> 02:06.007
[♪ opening theme song playing]

02:17.936 --> 02:20.522
THE LAID-OFF CHEAT-GRANTING MAGE
ENJOYS A SECOND LEASE ON LIFE

03:34.012 --> 03:35.097
NO. 1 ADVENTURING GEAR SHOP

03:35.222 --> 03:37.140
[LILY AND REIN] Bokenman!

03:38.225 --> 03:40.559
[LILY] <i>With over 100 locations
across the nation,</i>

03:40.560 --> 03:43.020
<i>this dependable specialty store
sells all manner of goods</i>

03:43.021 --> 03:44.940
<i>for adventurers
and other experts in the field.</i>

03:45.315 --> 03:47.149
<i>Did I mention that
the store also manages</i>

03:47.150 --> 03:49.193
<i>its own shipping,
production, and sales?</i>

03:49.194 --> 03:50.611
<i>There are no middlemen!</i>

03:50.612 --> 03:52.780
[REIN] <i>Is that why they can
offer high-quality products</i>

03:52.781 --> 03:54.782
<i>to consumers at low, low prices?</i>

03:54.783 --> 03:56.701
[LILY] <i>That's right, Rein!
When you enter a store,</i>

03:56.702 --> 03:59.745
<i>don't let the shock give you
a massive coronary!</i>

03:59.746 --> 04:01.956
- [EMPLOYEE] <i>Welcome in.</i>
- [REIN] <i>Look at all this</i>

04:01.957 --> 04:03.708
<i>top-of-the-line
adventuring gear!</i>

04:03.709 --> 04:05.292
[LILY] <i>You wouldn't expect
anything less</i>

04:05.293 --> 04:07.503
<i>from such a major company!
So come on down!</i>

04:07.504 --> 04:09.839
<i>You're guaranteed
to find something you like!</i>

04:09.840 --> 04:11.425
[REIN] <i>Excited! Excited!</i>

04:12.009 --> 04:14.469
<i>Everything's so amazing,
I can't choose.</i>

04:15.345 --> 04:17.680
- What do you think of this?
- [LILY] Looks good to me!

04:17.681 --> 04:19.181
- [Rein chuckles]
- [LILY] Ha!

04:19.182 --> 04:20.683
- [Rein chuckles]
- [Lily grunts]

04:20.684 --> 04:23.185
- [Rein laughs]
- [LILY] Hm. [groans]

04:23.186 --> 04:24.311
[snores]

04:24.312 --> 04:26.814
[REIN] Lily, I think
I found the one.

04:26.815 --> 04:28.441
Huh? Let's see.

04:28.442 --> 04:30.359
That's what
you're always wearing.

04:30.360 --> 04:32.945
I waited ages
for such a lame visual gag?

04:32.946 --> 04:34.196
[Rein screaming]

04:34.197 --> 04:36.073
[LILY] You still have them on!

04:36.074 --> 04:37.074
WE KILL PEOPLE

04:37.075 --> 04:38.451
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
Here you are, Mirabelle!

04:38.452 --> 04:40.161
Have some omelet rice.

04:40.162 --> 04:42.455
You love omelet rice, don't you?

04:42.456 --> 04:43.664
- [BROTHER 1] Yay!
- [BROTHER 2] Omelet rice!

04:43.665 --> 04:45.417
[MIRABELLE'S MOM] Lately, we've
been having it for every meal,

04:45.542 --> 04:47.877
so we'd be ready
whenever you showed up.

04:47.878 --> 04:49.086
[laughs]

04:49.087 --> 04:51.505
We knew that
you'd be home sooner or later,

04:51.506 --> 04:53.299
but I just wanted you to see
how I would do

04:53.300 --> 04:55.718
- absolutely anything for you.
- Thanks, Mom.

04:55.719 --> 04:57.219
We're about to lose our minds

04:57.220 --> 04:58.929
over this omelet rice
marathon from hell.

04:58.930 --> 04:59.930
You've got no idea

04:59.931 --> 05:01.140
how freaking glad
we are it's over.

05:01.141 --> 05:02.975
We've eaten enough
for 10 lifetimes.

05:02.976 --> 05:04.101
- R-I-P!
- We're finally free

05:04.102 --> 05:05.686
from the shackles
of omelet rice.

05:05.687 --> 05:06.896
I'd rather be an otaku

05:06.897 --> 05:08.189
than eat another helping
of that crap!

05:08.190 --> 05:09.190
Shut your traps.

05:09.191 --> 05:11.734
Are you boys trying
to destroy our family's peace?

05:11.735 --> 05:14.111
Maybe we have ourselves
a food fight?

05:14.112 --> 05:15.863
[laughter]

05:15.864 --> 05:17.741
Wow, you guys.

05:18.241 --> 05:20.242
Well, what are you waiting for?

05:20.243 --> 05:21.535
We can't have our dinner

05:21.536 --> 05:23.496
until you wash your hands
and gargle.

05:23.497 --> 05:24.498
Right!

05:28.502 --> 05:30.295
[MIRABELLE] The water's so cold.

05:31.838 --> 05:33.256
- [BROTHER 1] Oh, Mirabelle.
- [MIRABELLE] Uh?

05:34.049 --> 05:35.299
What is it?

05:35.300 --> 05:38.094
Mom told us that
yesterday was your birthday.

05:38.095 --> 05:39.512
We missed it so...

05:39.513 --> 05:41.305
We all pitched in
and got you a present!

05:41.306 --> 05:42.932
- [BOTH] Yeah.
- Something real nice.

05:42.933 --> 05:44.225
You're gonna be so surprised.

05:44.226 --> 05:46.352
[chuckles] A gift? What is it?

05:46.353 --> 05:47.478
[BROTHER 2] This.

05:47.479 --> 05:48.479
[gasps]

05:48.480 --> 05:50.439
[BROTHER 3] A high-end
stabby-stabby murder knife.

05:50.440 --> 05:52.067
It's super sharp, we tested it.

05:52.192 --> 05:53.526
[BROTHER 4]
Use it to kill lots of people

05:53.527 --> 05:54.568
and make Mom happy.

05:54.569 --> 05:56.570
We've gotta keep
our eight-person assassin family

05:56.571 --> 05:57.656
from falling apart.

05:58.532 --> 06:00.157
- [Mirabelle grunts]
- [BROTHER 1] What's wrong?

06:00.158 --> 06:02.660
Guys, what if she doesn't like
what we got for her?

06:02.661 --> 06:04.912
Maybe you missed the part
about how we all pitched in.

06:04.913 --> 06:07.373
- You're so ungrateful!
- Why do you want to make us sad?

06:07.374 --> 06:09.625
We shower you with love
and this is what we get?

06:09.626 --> 06:12.504
Fine, we'll never do anything
nice for you ever again!

06:14.756 --> 06:16.465
[BROTHER 2]
What's going on with you?

06:16.466 --> 06:17.551
♪

06:22.806 --> 06:25.141
It's lovely. Thank you so much.

06:25.142 --> 06:27.059
[BROTHER 2] Whew,
don't scare us like that.

06:27.060 --> 06:28.352
[BROTHER 3] You had us going.

06:28.353 --> 06:29.729
[BROTHER 4]
Are those tears of joy?

06:29.730 --> 06:32.648
Whenever I'm having a hard time,
I'll just look at this

06:32.649 --> 06:34.942
and cheer up
since I'll be thinking of you!

06:34.943 --> 06:35.943
[brothers chattering]

06:35.944 --> 06:37.945
[birds chirping]

06:37.946 --> 06:39.865
[Acorn exclaiming]

06:40.824 --> 06:42.867
So, what am I looking at?

06:42.868 --> 06:44.285
Why only the first step

06:44.286 --> 06:46.412
in my ever-ascending
new career path!

06:46.413 --> 06:47.455
CORN DOGS
BARRIUS'S KITCHEN

06:47.456 --> 06:49.373
Welcome to my food truck.

06:49.374 --> 06:50.791
Uh...

06:50.792 --> 06:51.876
What?

06:51.877 --> 06:53.085
Losing my old job

06:53.086 --> 06:54.920
was the best thing
that happened to me.

06:54.921 --> 06:57.381
Now I can pursue my real dream.

06:57.382 --> 07:00.092
And I wanted you to be
my very first customer.

07:00.093 --> 07:02.386
[MARGARET]
Um, don't you have any friends?

07:02.387 --> 07:04.431
I wouldn't say
we're friends exactly,

07:04.556 --> 07:05.639
unless you wanna be.

07:05.640 --> 07:07.434
Think of this
as a sign of my support.

07:08.185 --> 07:10.394
Fine, I'll take
one corn dog then.

07:10.395 --> 07:13.439
What? Don't tell me
that you're only getting one.

07:13.440 --> 07:14.440
[MARGARET] Huh?

07:14.441 --> 07:16.942
Doesn't your delightful
little friend want one, too?

07:16.943 --> 07:18.235
Haven't you heard
it's not healthy

07:18.236 --> 07:19.904
to feed human food to dogs?

07:19.905 --> 07:22.199
Is human food healthy
for humans?

07:22.366 --> 07:23.491
Here you go.

07:23.492 --> 07:26.328
Wow, that looks really tasty.

07:27.204 --> 07:28.705
NOM NOM NOM

07:29.289 --> 07:31.499
- Go on. It's good, right?
- No offense,

07:31.500 --> 07:33.417
but it's kinda difficult
to screw up a corn dog,

07:33.418 --> 07:35.461
- even for you.
- [barks]

07:35.462 --> 07:36.670
[BARRIUS] Aw...

07:36.671 --> 07:38.172
Thanks for the food.

07:38.173 --> 07:39.215
[Acorn whining]

07:39.216 --> 07:41.175
[BARRIUS] You heard the latest
about the Blue Crystals?

07:41.176 --> 07:44.011
They took a dangerous quest
for the cash.

07:44.012 --> 07:47.181
Now they're going around
and recruiting new members.

07:47.182 --> 07:50.101
Oh? Then they're
even more understaffed

07:50.102 --> 07:51.561
than I originally thought.

07:52.187 --> 07:53.771
Anyway, they had their chance

07:53.772 --> 07:55.606
but opted to lie
to get rid of me.

07:55.607 --> 07:58.443
If they're gonna act like that,
they must not be too desperate.

07:59.236 --> 08:01.195
- [Barrius sighs]
- [barks]

08:01.196 --> 08:02.823
[BARRIUS] Why are you like this?

08:03.990 --> 08:05.908
Well, I guess
we should be going.

08:05.909 --> 08:07.952
Thanks again, food truck man.

08:07.953 --> 08:09.370
- [indistinct chatter]
- [MIRABELLE'S MOM] Mirabelle,

08:09.371 --> 08:11.373
why don't you come
help me clean up?

08:16.253 --> 08:17.379
Mirabelle.

08:18.755 --> 08:19.964
Hey, Mom.

08:19.965 --> 08:22.384
Huh? What's the matter?

08:23.635 --> 08:24.928
Don't hate me...

08:25.470 --> 08:28.723
but I'm finished killing.

08:28.724 --> 08:32.435
And where did all this soft talk
come from all of a sudden?

08:32.436 --> 08:34.770
You got some cotton candy
stuck in your teeth?

08:34.771 --> 08:36.063
No, I really mean it.

08:36.064 --> 08:37.482
[all gasping]

08:38.358 --> 08:39.860
I've had enough.

08:42.320 --> 08:44.238
I smelled a coward
in this family,

08:44.239 --> 08:46.532
but instead of one
of your brothers, it was you.

08:46.533 --> 08:48.409
- I'll beat you back into shape.
- [whimpers]

08:48.410 --> 08:50.411
First, take off your glasses.

08:50.412 --> 08:52.246
But I'm not wearing any glasses.

08:52.247 --> 08:55.666
Oh? Perfect, so I can launch
right into giving you

08:55.667 --> 08:57.461
the worst beating of your life!

08:58.170 --> 09:00.255
I'm not trying
to start a fight with you!

09:03.091 --> 09:05.509
- [gasping]
- You screwing with me, kid?

09:05.510 --> 09:07.386
What makes you think
you can escape me

09:07.387 --> 09:10.056
with the Ultra Lightning Thunder
teleportation technique

09:10.057 --> 09:11.515
when I'm the one
who taught it to you

09:11.516 --> 09:12.767
in the first place?

09:12.768 --> 09:16.020
WE KILL PEOPLE

09:16.021 --> 09:17.814
[insects trilling]

09:20.275 --> 09:22.986
[groaning softly]

09:27.783 --> 09:30.702
SCIENCE
MIRABELLE

09:32.662 --> 09:34.206
- [REIN] There she is!
- [gasps]

09:34.664 --> 09:36.625
Hey, it's us, Mirabelle.

09:37.459 --> 09:39.418
You guys found me?

09:39.419 --> 09:41.921
[REIN] Whoa!
What in the hay happened here?

09:41.922 --> 09:44.215
[MIRABELLE] It's nothing.
Don't worry about it.

09:44.216 --> 09:46.258
This is obviously not nothing!

09:46.259 --> 09:47.551
[yelps, thuds]

09:47.552 --> 09:48.594
[LILY] Kind of hard helping

09:48.595 --> 09:50.304
when you've got
a broken arm and leg.

09:50.305 --> 09:52.808
- Let me do it.
- [REIN] Thanks a lot, Lily.

09:54.601 --> 09:57.521
[Mirabelle crying softly]

09:59.231 --> 10:01.108
- [REIN] Uh?
- [LILY] Hmm.

10:02.317 --> 10:04.151
- [MIRABELLE'S MOM] Mirabelle!
- Uh?

10:04.152 --> 10:08.155
I'm sorry you forced me
to get so angry!

10:08.156 --> 10:10.282
It's like you enjoy
making me lose my temper,

10:10.283 --> 10:11.910
my precious sunflower!

10:14.538 --> 10:17.373
So, who're these slack-jawed,
dead-eyed scumbags

10:17.374 --> 10:18.958
who look like
they get off talking shit

10:18.959 --> 10:20.334
behind other people's backs?

10:20.335 --> 10:23.045
If you've got a problem,
say it to my face,

10:23.046 --> 10:24.588
and I'll beat your ass.

10:24.589 --> 10:27.384
Talking shit is like
an endless supply of free opium

10:27.509 --> 10:29.010
for gloomy
and envious sons of bi--

10:29.011 --> 10:31.012
BUT THAT'S NOT STEROIDS...

10:31.013 --> 10:33.932
YOU'RE NOT ACTUALLY
THE SLIGHTEST BIT STRONGER!

10:35.017 --> 10:36.183
[MIRABELLE] Mama.

10:36.184 --> 10:37.768
[REIN]
You're Mirabelle's mother?

10:37.769 --> 10:39.228
So what if I am?

10:39.229 --> 10:41.439
You look like some filthy,
pathetic little pervert

10:41.440 --> 10:42.773
starved for boobs
and acceptance.

10:42.774 --> 10:44.442
Boobs? Now hold on.

10:44.443 --> 10:46.277
Look at you. I bet you're
even interested

10:46.278 --> 10:48.904
in my old lady snatch,
you sick little puppy.

10:48.905 --> 10:50.031
[REIN] Subject change!

10:50.032 --> 10:52.158
Why are Mirabelle's things
thrown all over the place?

10:52.159 --> 10:53.284
You know what?

10:53.285 --> 10:55.411
You're so scrawny,
you look like a middle schooler!

10:55.412 --> 10:58.539
And I bet that shitty haircut
only cost 1,000 yen.

10:58.540 --> 11:01.292
Ah! Well, even if
that is weirdly accurate,

11:01.293 --> 11:03.377
at least I know the proper way
to treat people.

11:03.378 --> 11:06.213
You come here and criticize
my parenting skills?

11:06.214 --> 11:08.049
I'll teach you a lesson.

11:08.050 --> 11:10.344
No, you don't wanna do that.

11:10.969 --> 11:14.348
[Rein gasps, screams]

11:14.931 --> 11:17.600
- Rein, no!
- [Mirabelle's mom screaming]

11:17.601 --> 11:20.603
What the hell did you do
to my hand?

11:20.604 --> 11:23.481
Sort of like punching
a brick wall at full speed, huh?

11:23.482 --> 11:26.525
Rein's defense
is the stuff of legend.

11:26.526 --> 11:28.235
He hasn't taken any damage.

11:28.236 --> 11:30.738
So he's some kind of freak?

11:30.739 --> 11:31.989
[Lily chuckles]

11:31.990 --> 11:34.325
We've got some
new adventures coming up

11:34.326 --> 11:35.868
and wanted to invite you along.

11:35.869 --> 11:37.204
[Mirabelle gasps]

11:37.996 --> 11:41.665
[LILY] We help each other
and watch our teammates' backs.

11:41.666 --> 11:44.752
Rein and I think you'd be
a good addition to the party.

11:44.753 --> 11:46.380
The party?

11:47.255 --> 11:49.174
- Mirabelle!
- [gasps]

11:49.633 --> 11:53.469
Did you forget about
your mother dying from pain?

11:53.470 --> 11:55.763
I'm gonna pass out
from how much my hand hurts.

11:55.764 --> 11:58.475
I need your help, dear. [cries]

12:00.936 --> 12:01.937
♪

12:03.689 --> 12:04.940
[MIRABELLE] Sorry, Lily.

12:05.691 --> 12:07.859
Apologize to Rein for me.

12:10.696 --> 12:12.530
We'll come back tomorrow.

12:12.531 --> 12:13.531
WE KILL PEOPLE

12:13.532 --> 12:15.450
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
What am I going to do with you?

12:16.159 --> 12:18.954
Do you realize this will take
months to fully heal?

12:19.705 --> 12:22.289
If it ever goes back to normal.

12:22.290 --> 12:24.209
I tried warning you.

12:24.918 --> 12:27.753
Oh, please. I'm used to it.

12:27.754 --> 12:30.506
It's a parent's job
to suffer endless indignities

12:30.507 --> 12:32.675
for her little rays of sunshine.

12:32.676 --> 12:34.344
Okay, Mom.

12:38.432 --> 12:41.143
- So, who were those two really?
- Uh?

12:41.643 --> 12:44.562
Funny enough, they're the people
Cornelius wanted dead.

12:44.563 --> 12:45.814
- I let them live.
- Huh?

12:46.398 --> 12:48.065
- That's hot!
- You what?

12:48.066 --> 12:49.567
Why didn't you kill them?

12:49.568 --> 12:50.776
Well, you see--

12:50.777 --> 12:52.445
I can't believe
you'd be stupid enough

12:52.446 --> 12:54.739
to embarrass me this badly!
[cries]

12:54.740 --> 12:55.990
Out of everyone here,

12:55.991 --> 12:58.409
I never thought
you'd be the one to betray me.

12:58.410 --> 13:00.911
I'm sorry, Mom.
I never meant to hurt you.

13:00.912 --> 13:02.788
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
You know I would do anything

13:02.789 --> 13:05.458
to protect you.
I'd leap into hell for you!

13:05.459 --> 13:08.086
Fight any enemy
to save your worthless skin!

13:08.587 --> 13:12.632
So why the hell would you go
and make life harder for me?

13:13.592 --> 13:16.135
I'm begging you from the bottom
of my heart, sweetie!

13:16.136 --> 13:17.428
Though I doubt
there's any point,

13:17.429 --> 13:20.348
could you try and love your
poor mother a teensy bit more?

13:20.349 --> 13:22.516
Is it really
so difficult for you

13:22.517 --> 13:25.811
to care about me
as much as I care about you?

13:25.812 --> 13:26.854
You're hurting me!

13:26.855 --> 13:28.607
♪

13:29.775 --> 13:32.985
- Uh?
- Forget it. Just leave me alone.

13:32.986 --> 13:34.529
I'm sorry.

13:36.156 --> 13:37.282
Mama?

13:38.116 --> 13:40.826
[CEO]
Margaret Ells, this is yours.

13:40.827 --> 13:42.704
You'll want
to read it carefully.

13:47.626 --> 13:49.669
Don't linger. Hurry up and go.

13:50.879 --> 13:51.962
Honestly...

13:51.963 --> 13:54.215
- Thanks for waiting, Acorn.
- [Acorn barks]

13:54.216 --> 13:55.966
[CEO] Your dog better not
have made a mess

13:55.967 --> 13:57.343
while it was in the hall.

13:57.344 --> 14:00.012
[MARGARET] Oh, him?
That's just the CEO, Acorn.

14:00.013 --> 14:01.972
Eek! So scary.

14:01.973 --> 14:04.558
Terrifying, I know,
and a humongous jerk.

14:04.559 --> 14:07.061
Get this, he thinks that
reciting the guild precepts

14:07.062 --> 14:08.354
makes us better adventurers.

14:08.355 --> 14:11.232
"Reciting guild precepts?"
Sounds dumb.

14:11.233 --> 14:13.526
"It's important
to say them aloud..."

14:13.527 --> 14:15.986
How much longer
do you plan on doing this bit?

14:15.987 --> 14:18.322
[EMPEROR'S SHIELDS' MEMBERS]
We are happy every day.

14:18.323 --> 14:20.950
We are grateful for adventures.

14:20.951 --> 14:23.662
Grateful! Grateful! Grateful!

14:24.037 --> 14:25.163
[Mirabelle's mom grunts]

14:26.081 --> 14:27.749
What nice weather we're having.

14:28.875 --> 14:32.920
Hey, flap it harder
or it'll wrinkle, idiot.

14:32.921 --> 14:35.589
I swear, if my hand
wasn't useless, I'd...

14:35.590 --> 14:37.008
- [footsteps]
- Huh?

14:37.634 --> 14:40.553
Why are you here?
Come back to kidnap my daughter?

14:40.554 --> 14:43.097
No way. But if you're going
to force Mirabelle

14:43.098 --> 14:45.057
to kill people
when she doesn't want to,

14:45.058 --> 14:46.934
then I, a D-rank adventurer...

14:46.935 --> 14:49.812
And I, an S-rank adventurer,
will make you stop.

14:49.813 --> 14:51.897
I'll scrape you pests
off my shoe!

14:51.898 --> 14:53.400
I head an eight-person family.

14:53.525 --> 14:55.818
I'm an X-rank assassin,
mature lady warrior!

14:55.819 --> 14:56.819
[both grunt]

14:56.820 --> 14:58.195
Hold on, Mom, don't fight.

14:58.196 --> 15:00.823
Taking their side over mine!
I should've known!

15:00.824 --> 15:02.241
I'm not choosing sides.

15:02.242 --> 15:04.869
It's just I love you
and Rein and Lily all equally.

15:04.870 --> 15:06.121
[grunts] Shut up.

15:06.872 --> 15:09.165
Hey, what was that for?

15:09.166 --> 15:12.001
I'm going to send both of you
to a deep, dark place

15:12.002 --> 15:13.919
for trying to make
a fool out of me.

15:13.920 --> 15:16.422
Starting with you,
thousand-yen haircut boy!

15:16.423 --> 15:19.425
Get ready to taste
my Super Ultra Lightning Hammer.

15:19.426 --> 15:20.801
But Mom, your hand...

15:20.802 --> 15:22.553
you said it would take months
for it to heal.

15:22.554 --> 15:24.555
[laughs]

15:24.556 --> 15:27.558
As if punching a small child
into the recesses of space

15:27.559 --> 15:29.518
was enough to sideline me.

15:29.519 --> 15:31.270
The suffering
wasn't a total lie,

15:31.271 --> 15:33.773
since I had to swallow my pride
to put on that performance

15:33.774 --> 15:35.816
to make you reflect
on your selfishness.

15:35.817 --> 15:39.362
Ha! I can't believe
you actually took me seriously.

15:39.363 --> 15:40.821
What an idiot.

15:40.822 --> 15:42.698
If you keep underestimating
your mother,

15:42.699 --> 15:43.783
I just might have to kill you...

15:43.784 --> 15:44.825
This whole time you were faking?

15:44.826 --> 15:46.786
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
I'm through playing games.

15:46.787 --> 15:48.788
I'm gonna hunt down
your whole family,

15:48.789 --> 15:51.792
all of your worthless friends,
even your guildmaster.

15:51.917 --> 15:53.626
And after I've rounded them up,

15:53.627 --> 15:55.878
I'm gonna Super Ultra
the lot of you!

15:55.879 --> 15:57.296
We won't let Elsie die.

15:57.297 --> 16:00.174
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
Huh? What did you say?

16:00.175 --> 16:02.176
<i>You mean that Elsie?</i>

16:02.177 --> 16:03.595
How do you know her?

16:04.096 --> 16:06.681
Turns out that little meddler's
involved, huh?

16:06.682 --> 16:08.557
I reckon slaughtering
that dumbass Rein

16:08.558 --> 16:11.519
would take at least one,
I'm ashamed to admit.

16:11.520 --> 16:15.731
Lily claims to be S-rank,
so that would probably take two.

16:15.732 --> 16:19.443
Elsie would need three,
and that's just for starters.

16:19.444 --> 16:21.196
The girl won't go down easily.

16:21.571 --> 16:23.739
She'd keep making things
difficult for me

16:23.740 --> 16:25.283
until she fully bled out.

16:25.409 --> 16:29.078
So that'll take
an extra one, two, three.

16:29.079 --> 16:30.956
Let me do some fast math here.

16:31.248 --> 16:32.957
That's six total.

16:32.958 --> 16:34.834
Sounds about right.

16:34.835 --> 16:35.752
Uh-huh...

16:36.628 --> 16:39.505
If keeping you around
costs me this much,

16:39.506 --> 16:42.216
it makes sense
that I can do without you.

16:42.217 --> 16:43.884
Plus, the other kids

16:43.885 --> 16:46.137
are starting to grow up,
so whatever!

16:46.138 --> 16:47.179
[MIRABELLE] Mama...

16:47.180 --> 16:49.558
Please don't turn your back
on me.

16:51.393 --> 16:54.395
You can have this one.
Do whatever you want with her.

16:54.396 --> 16:55.730
[BOTH] Mirabelle.

16:55.731 --> 16:58.441
But you said you'd do anything
to protect me!

16:58.442 --> 17:02.069
How you'd even leap
into fiery pits! You love me!

17:02.070 --> 17:04.740
This doesn't make sense.
Why are you doing this?

17:05.073 --> 17:07.867
[MIRABELLE'S MOM] Hey, kids,
gather around. Time to eat.

17:07.868 --> 17:10.202
What?
You put out too many plates.

17:10.203 --> 17:11.537
[BROTHER 1]
But there's eight of us.

17:11.538 --> 17:12.705
[BROTHER 2]
Eight is right, right?

17:12.706 --> 17:14.540
[MIRABELLE'S MOM] What the hell
are you talking about?

17:14.541 --> 17:16.709
We're a seven-person family now.

17:16.710 --> 17:17.793
[gasps]

17:17.794 --> 17:19.837
- Don't say that.
- Mirabelle.

17:19.838 --> 17:21.589
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
This is my house!

17:21.590 --> 17:22.840
Get out, haircut!

17:22.841 --> 17:24.467
You've got no problem
getting angry!

17:24.468 --> 17:27.219
So why can't you use it to fight
for Mirabelle just once?

17:27.220 --> 17:29.347
You've got no right
to lecture me.

17:29.348 --> 17:31.016
Hey, Mom,
are we gonna get dinner?

17:31.141 --> 17:33.017
- We're hungry.
- How ungrateful.

17:33.018 --> 17:34.560
Don't you stand there sniveling

17:34.561 --> 17:36.854
like I've been depriving you
for days on end.

17:36.855 --> 17:39.565
Damn it! Do I have to do
everything around here?

17:39.566 --> 17:41.108
You can all eat shit.

17:41.109 --> 17:42.610
Don't do this.

17:42.611 --> 17:44.196
I love you, Mom.

17:44.863 --> 17:47.491
- [cries]
- [knife thudding]

17:51.578 --> 17:53.954
[MIRABELLE'S MOM]
Rein! Lily! Elsie!

17:53.955 --> 17:56.332
Rein! Lily! Elsie!

17:56.333 --> 17:59.335
Just you wait. Dead.
You're all dead.

17:59.336 --> 18:03.089
Rein! Lily! Elsie!

18:03.090 --> 18:06.426
[MIRABELLE] Thank you
for everything you've given me.

18:09.304 --> 18:11.347
[BARRIUS]
All right. One corn dog.

18:11.348 --> 18:12.348
[BOTH] Huh?

18:12.349 --> 18:14.600
- Order up.
- Stop slacking.

18:14.601 --> 18:16.769
You're making your customers
wait way too long.

18:16.770 --> 18:19.730
Stop acting like
you were waiting for hours. Huh?

18:19.731 --> 18:20.691
EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT
MARGARET ELLS

18:20.816 --> 18:21.899
What you got there?

18:21.900 --> 18:24.026
This? You can
take a look if you want.

18:24.027 --> 18:25.194
What's that? You'll give me

18:25.195 --> 18:26.987
an entire year's supply
of free corn dogs

18:26.988 --> 18:28.823
to say thanks
for such an epic opportunity?

18:28.824 --> 18:30.658
Can you afford
to be so generous?

18:30.659 --> 18:32.201
On second thought,
don't answer that.

18:32.202 --> 18:34.704
Yeah, yeah, shut up. Huh?

18:34.705 --> 18:37.790
- Is this a contract?
- The Emperor's Shields prefer

18:37.791 --> 18:39.709
to keep their adventurers
exclusive.

18:39.710 --> 18:41.544
The contracts last
for three years,

18:41.545 --> 18:42.962
and mine is up for renewal.

18:42.963 --> 18:45.882
Oh, we're going
through this again?

18:46.299 --> 18:48.843
Despite that vacant expression,
you do realize

18:48.844 --> 18:50.970
that you should join
the Blue Crystals, don't you?

18:50.971 --> 18:51.971
[MARGARET] Uh?

18:51.972 --> 18:54.223
Again with that?
Stop being gross.

18:54.224 --> 18:56.100
You're already bald,
and that's bad enough.

18:56.101 --> 18:57.811
- You're really testing me.
- Uh?

18:58.770 --> 19:00.938
I'm sorry you made me
call you bald and gross.

19:00.939 --> 19:02.273
That's not the problem.

19:02.274 --> 19:04.275
How long are you gonna
keep running?

19:04.276 --> 19:06.444
Get over there
and ask them to let you join.

19:06.445 --> 19:08.070
- [MARGARET] Mmm.
- [Acorn grunts]

19:08.071 --> 19:10.156
[BARRIUS] I know it's not
the easiest thing,

19:10.157 --> 19:12.616
but you can't drag your feet
forever, you know?

19:12.617 --> 19:14.452
Now, feel free to call me bald.

19:14.453 --> 19:16.454
- Baldy.
- Cut it out.

19:16.455 --> 19:19.623
- Ugh, damn.
- Wait a sec. Get back here.

19:19.624 --> 19:21.667
I'm being followed
by a strange man.

19:21.668 --> 19:23.711
Also, you've got no right
to criticize me, dude.

19:23.712 --> 19:25.504
I'm an innocent customer
at your food truck

19:25.505 --> 19:27.631
looking for corn dogs,
not life advice.

19:27.632 --> 19:29.550
[panting]

19:29.551 --> 19:30.844
Use your words.

19:31.553 --> 19:33.220
You're right, I was wrong.

19:33.221 --> 19:34.972
Wait, so you're just
agreeing with me?

19:34.973 --> 19:36.724
Maybe the basis
of our relationship

19:36.725 --> 19:39.101
is centered around delicious
and affordable corn dogs.

19:39.102 --> 19:40.770
But like any other
decent human being,

19:40.771 --> 19:43.230
I want you to stop
depriving yourself of happiness.

19:43.231 --> 19:45.149
[mocking]

19:45.150 --> 19:46.359
[BARRIUS] Stop making fun.

19:46.360 --> 19:49.362
Margaret, when are you joining
the Blue Crystals?

19:49.363 --> 19:50.404
[both mocking]

19:50.405 --> 19:52.324
[BARRIUS] And how long
are you gonna keep doing that?

19:53.408 --> 19:54.659
[thudding]

19:55.410 --> 19:57.161
[panting]

19:57.162 --> 19:59.081
- [footsteps]
- Huh?

20:00.415 --> 20:01.665
What's with the branch?

20:01.666 --> 20:03.626
Well, uh,
if I touch you directly,

20:03.627 --> 20:06.420
I'll get sweat and grease
and weird shit all over me.

20:06.421 --> 20:08.340
Come on,
am I really that filthy?

20:10.258 --> 20:12.593
Look, I'm gonna hold on
to your contract,

20:12.594 --> 20:14.595
at least
for the rest of the day.

20:14.596 --> 20:17.431
In the meantime, take a minute
to think about your future.

20:17.432 --> 20:20.685
But all I can think about now
is how you touched my contract.

20:20.686 --> 20:21.853
[groans]

20:22.604 --> 20:25.231
[MARGARET]
Yeah, yeah, but do me a favor.

20:25.232 --> 20:27.983
Have something
other than corn dogs tomorrow.

20:27.984 --> 20:29.069
[BARRIUS] Promise.

20:29.486 --> 20:30.821
You'd better show up.

20:31.947 --> 20:34.032
- [Margaret giggling]
- [barking]

20:36.952 --> 20:39.954
[MARGARET] Wait up, Acorn.
Not so fast.

20:39.955 --> 20:41.373
♪

20:46.670 --> 20:48.629
- [THUG] Hey.
- Hmm?

20:48.630 --> 20:50.923
Hi, it's great
to see you fellas.

20:50.924 --> 20:52.634
How is everyone doing?

20:53.010 --> 20:54.760
[Margaret chuckling]

20:54.761 --> 20:56.930
[laughing]

21:00.267 --> 21:02.561
[♪ closing theme song playing]

22:32.651 --> 22:35.444
Hey, miss,
you want to get paid for sex?

22:35.445 --> 22:37.489
You can make a lot for us.

22:38.031 --> 22:40.575
So then, they're the THUGs.

22:41.618 --> 22:44.161
<i>Freed from the constraints
of their guild,</i>

22:44.162 --> 22:46.331
<i>they've turned
to a life of crime.</i>

22:46.915 --> 22:48.332
<i>It's only a matter of time</i>

22:48.333 --> 22:49.792
<i>before they see
Rein's enchantments</i>

22:49.793 --> 22:51.670
<i>as a viable source of income.</i>

22:52.170 --> 22:54.339
<i>I have to keep an eye on them.</i>

22:59.261 --> 23:01.430
You can depend on us.

23:03.724 --> 23:05.016
[woman screaming]

23:05.017 --> 23:06.935
[THUG 1] Aw, come on!
Get back here!

23:07.519 --> 23:08.854
[screaming continues]

23:09.354 --> 23:11.273
[ELSIE] <i>They've placed
their trust in me.</i>

23:12.566 --> 23:14.316
<i>I should do the same.</i>...

23:14.317 --> 23:16.236
<i>and have faith
in their strength.</i>

23:18.989 --> 23:20.322
[thugs screaming]

23:20.323 --> 23:22.534
[both groaning]

23:23.994 --> 23:25.494
I've made my decision.

23:25.495 --> 23:26.912
I'll stay in town

23:26.913 --> 23:29.290
and eliminate whoever stands
in their way,

23:29.291 --> 23:30.916
so they can focus entirely

23:30.917 --> 23:33.295
on adventuring
free of any obstacles.

23:33.712 --> 23:34.921
That is my job...

23:35.839 --> 23:38.175
as the Blue Crystals'
guildmaster.
